---
// The tab convention, stated once, on every page that has tabs.
//
// Three ways, not two: a page that shows only the prompt and the clicks leaves
// the reader who works from a terminal or the API with nothing.
//
// TAB LABEL CONTRACT — these three strings, byte for byte, on every page:
//
//     Prompt        UI        CLI / API
//
// Starlight's <Tabs syncKey="howto"> remembers the reader's choice in
// localStorage under the *label text*, so a page that spells a label
// differently silently drops out of the sync and resets the reader.
//
// Plan mode, measured in two staged runs: it adds
// one approval of a written plan and then asks for every change exactly as
// before: 8 approvals to the control run's 7. It is a review gate, not a way
// to approve once, and the hub's #approvals-and-plan-mode, which the undo line
// links, says so.
//
// Every task page carries three tabs; `write/` keeps two, so
// both shapes exist. `manual={false}` swaps in a lead that still names all
// three tabs: on app/ an earlier version let it win over `tabs={3}` and hide
// the CLI tab from the reader entirely.
//
// The wording lives in ./pathintro.mjs (pathIntroHtml), next to the fuller
// plain-text version the markdown twin prints, because the twin has to carry
// the "these are alternatives" sentence too: without it, an agent reads the
// three flattened sections as three things to do in sequence.
// scripts/pathintro.test.ts holds the two to the same facts.
//
// Three short lines instead of three paragraphs, which put 179 words on every
// task page. The approvals, tool
// permissions and plan mode detail moved to the hub, under "How every page
// works", where every page links; the twin keeps the full wording.
//
// Usage:  <PathIntro tabs={3} />              — Prompt · UI · CLI / API
//         <PathIntro />                       — legacy two-tab wording
//         <PathIntro approvals={false} />     — read-only pages, where it does not
//         <PathIntro manual={false} />        — no click-by-click equivalent exists
//         <PathIntro yours="the Google consent screen" />

import { pathIntroHtml } from './pathintro.mjs';

const paragraphs = pathIntroHtml(Astro.props);
---

<div class="gs-pathintro">
  {paragraphs.map((p) => <p class={p.recovery ? 'gs-pathintro__recovery' : undefined} set:html={p.html} />)}
</div>
